# Functional requirements

**Canonical source:** [docs/FRD.md](../../docs/FRD.md)

## Before implementing

For any **feature**, **behavior change**, or **user-visible fix** that affects what the app does:

1. Read `docs/FRD.md` (use `@docs/FRD.md` when helpful).
2. If the behavior is **missing or ambiguous**, stop: agree functionality with the user and **update the FRD first**—then implement.

## After implementing

Update `docs/FRD.md` in the **same** change set (same PR/session):

- **Today** — when shipped behavior changes or new capability ships.
- **Planned** — when roadmap intent changes; move items from Planned to Today when implemented.

Keep **value-led, customer-facing** narrative (why + what). Do not turn the FRD into a field list, technical spec, or copy-compliance doc.

## Scope

- **FRD:** what the product does and will do.
- **Copy/compliance:** [docs/COPY-GUIDELINES.md](../../docs/COPY-GUIDELINES.md) via `terminology-compliance.mdc`.
- **Technical how-to:** other `.cursor/rules/` files (architecture, thermal export, tests, etc.).

Do not duplicate FRD content into rules or README feature lists.
